# Inventory Management Module — Implementation Plan

## Overview

Add a full **Inventory Management** module to the Home Art Furniture platform. This module tracks raw materials and supplies used in custom furniture builds (wood, fabric, hardware, adhesives, etc.), manages supplier relationships, records stock-in/stock-out transactions, and provides low-stock alerts on the dashboard.

The module follows the exact same architectural patterns as the existing `orders`, `customers`, and `measurements` apps: function-based views, a `services.py` layer for business logic, Tailwind-based dark-mode templates extending `base.html`, and `django.test.TestCase` tests.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Material Categories** — Should material categories (Wood, Fabric, Hardware, Paint, Adhesive, etc.) be a fixed `TextChoices` enum (like `FurnitureType`), or should they be user-configurable via a DB table (like `CustomFurnitureType`)? I recommend **fixed enum + custom DB table** (same hybrid approach as measurements).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Purchase Orders** — Do you want a full Purchase Order workflow (Create PO → Send to Supplier → Receive Goods → Close PO), or is a simpler "Record Stock In" form sufficient for now? I recommend **starting with simple stock-in/stock-out transactions** and adding POs later.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Order-Inventory Linkage** — Should we link inventory consumption to specific orders (e.g., "Order HAF-20260714-001 used 2m² of teak wood"), or is the inventory module standalone for now? I recommend **standalone first**, with linkage as a future enhancement.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q4: Units of Measurement** — Materials will need different units (kg, meters, sq.ft, pieces, liters, sheets). Should units be a fixed enum or user-configurable? I recommend **fixed enum** covering the common units.

