### Phase 3: Services Layer

#### [NEW] [services.py](file:///c:/Projects/HomeArtFurniture/inventory/services.py)

Business logic functions following the `orders/services.py` pattern:

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `record_stock_in(material, qty, unit_cost, supplier, reference, notes, date)` | Creates a `STOCK_IN` transaction, updates `material.current_stock += qty` |
| `record_stock_out(material, qty, reference, notes, date)` | Creates a `STOCK_OUT` transaction, validates sufficient stock, updates `material.current_stock -= qty` |
| `record_adjustment(material, new_qty, notes, date)` | Creates an `ADJUSTMENT` transaction with delta, sets `material.current_stock = new_qty` |
| `record_damage(material, qty, notes, date)` | Creates a `DAMAGED` transaction, updates `material.current_stock -= qty` |
| `create_material_from_post(post_data)` | Parses form POST data, validates, creates `Material` |
| `update_material_from_post(material, post_data)` | Parses form POST data, validates, updates `Material` |
| `create_supplier_from_post(post_data)` | Parses form POST data, creates `Supplier` |
| `update_supplier_from_post(supplier, post_data)` | Updates `Supplier` from POST |

All stock mutations wrapped in `@transaction.atomic` with proper validation.

